<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sheraton Move</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2020</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sheraton Move was the political manoeuvre of February 2020 that brought down Malaysia's Pakatan Harapan government. Defecting members of parliament and opposition parties met at the Sheraton hotel in Petaling Jaya, Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahathir-mohamad">Mahathir Mohamad</a> resigned, and Muhyiddin Yassin was appointed prime minister at the head of a new coalition, Perikatan Nasional.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sheraton-move.jpg" alt="Sheraton Move" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This vector image includes elements that have been taken or adapted from this file: · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Malaysia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
